VALUES ('28cb28ae-b558-4907-aa3a-4c908671b282', 'NC17.1.G.2', 2, 'numeric', 'Name the parts of a composite shape (sides, corners, faces)', 'Tara puts a triangle on top of a square. All 3 sides of the triangle are the same length as a side of the square. One side of the triangle fits exactly on the top side of the square. How many sides does the new shape have?', '[]', '5', '3+2', 'The square has 4 sides, but its top side is now covered. The sides left are 3 from the square. The triangle adds 2 sides on top. That is 3 + 2 = 5 sides.', 'checked', '{"lint":[],"solve":{"answer":"5","agreed":true,"single_answer":true,"aligned":true,"grade_appropriate":true,"error_free":true,"issues":"","work":"Equilateral triangle on the top of the square: outline has bottom, 2 square sides, 2 triangle sides = 5 (no sides line up since 60+90 is not 180).","run_id":"claude-code","at":"2026-10-24T08:32:29.359Z"}}', 'ai', NULL, NULL)
