VALUES ('0df1179d-069b-48d9-b103-7b9670ca4f0a', 'NC17.4.NBT.5', 3, 'choice', 'Partial products', 'Dev finds $62 \times 35$ by adding $62 \times 5 = 310$ and $62 \times 3 = 186$. His answer is wrong. What is the correct product?', '["496","1860","2480","2170"]', '2170', '62*35', 'The 3 in 35 means 30, so the second partial product is $62 \times 30 = 1860$. Then $310 + 1860 = 2170$.', 'checked', '{"lint":[],"solve":{"answer":"2170","agreed":true,"single_answer":true,"aligned":true,"grade_appropriate":true,"error_free":true,"issues":"","work":"62 x 35 = 62x30 + 62x5 = 1860 + 310 = 2170 (Dev used 62x3 not 62x30).","run_id":"claude-code","at":"2026-10-24T03:07:42.830Z"}}', 'ai', NULL, NULL)
